#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 900.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060507} :activity/id #uuid "cfab7801-e5d9-5cc5-82dd-9b1700800489" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049773} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060507 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060889 :tutorial/content "The following two identities are known as the **sum and difference formulas for sine**:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}(x+y) & =\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{cos}y+\\operatorname{cos}x\\operatorname{sin}y \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}(x-y) & =\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{cos}y-\\operatorname{cos}x\\operatorname{sin}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe'll prove these results at the end of the lesson.\n\nThese identities can be used to calculate the sine of an angle which is the sum or difference of two special angles. \n\nFor example, we can use the sum rule to find the exact value of $\\sin(75^\\circ).$ We start by writing $75^\\circ$ as a sum of special angles:\n\n$$\n75^\\circ = {\\color{blue}45^\\circ} + {\\color{red}30^\\circ}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the sum formula for sine as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}{75}^{∘} & =\\operatorname{sin}({45}^{∘}+{30}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}{45}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}{30}^{∘}+\\operatorname{cos}{45}^{∘}\\operatorname{sin}{30}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\sin 75^\\circ =   \\dfrac {\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}} 4.\n$$\n\nLet's see another example." :tutorial/id #uuid "a8b2cde2-4c10-51d6-b6f7-3b2a941a1d98" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2559 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "1a9ccd10-0e50-5e86-b3d2-338000cdb1c8" :step/math-academy-id 11728 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060509}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060508 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059662 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059493 :question/id #uuid "4cd24c10-1838-5f4b-ac88-cfbfc2ec4c21" :question/math-academy-id "e-3518" :question/problem "Express $\\sin\\left(x - 30^{\\circ} \\right )$ in terms of $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(u-v) = \\sin u\\cos v - \\cos u\\sin v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v=30^{\\circ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{30}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "69e91ce7-259a-5a11-bb79-7e6ad7ea86d4" :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749448} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060120} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060352} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233843} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233848} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233849} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272252} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272253} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272254} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272255} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272256} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292752} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304991} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304992} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304993} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304994} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701658} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701660} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701661} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701793} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701797} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701807} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701813} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701817} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705267} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705269} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705309} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705311} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705312} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705320} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749415} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749417} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749423} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749430} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749431} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749434} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749438} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749440} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749443}] :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expressions in Degrees Using the Sum and Difference Formulas"} :step/id #uuid "08e66865-9eab-589a-a7af-77b1058ad01d" :step/math-academy-id 11729 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060759}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060509 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059663 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059494 :question/id #uuid "7341638b-3c0f-5c10-8b7d-a2c313607bed" :question/math-academy-id "e-3519" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)$ without using a calculator.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $$\n\\displaystyle \\dfrac{\\pi}{12} = \\dfrac{\\pi}{3} - \\dfrac{\\pi}{4}.\n$$*" :question/worked-solution "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(x-y) = \\sin x\\cos y - \\cos x\\sin y\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $x = \\dfrac{\\pi}{3}$ and $y = \\dfrac{\\pi}{4},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "213eda96-c41d-5361-9da9-8349617014f1" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049923} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050848}] :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701936} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060002} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060103} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233846} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233847} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253530} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292748} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335834} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335835} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701916} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701917} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701919} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701924} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701934} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705137} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705143} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705144} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705148} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705190} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705211} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705213} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705214} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705254} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705257} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705264}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Values Using the Sum and Difference Formulas"} :step/id #uuid "a3de70e8-719f-5346-882f-897c95f91dfb" :step/math-academy-id 11732 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060508}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060759 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059820 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059627 :question/id #uuid "0ce71d86-7470-5d53-ac94-20b473889dee" :question/math-academy-id "e-9983" :question/problem "Express $\\sin\\left(x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{6} \\right)$ in terms of $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(u+v) = \\sin{u}\\cos{v} + \\cos{u}\\sin{v}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum formula for sine with $u = x$ and $v = \\dfrac{\\pi}{6},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b12a7b7-1df3-5203-934e-8820604de3de" :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701968} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060109} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060281} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233451} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233585} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233844} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233850} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233851} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272257} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272258} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272322} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272323} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304795} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304996} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304998} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304999} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335836} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701780} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701791} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701792} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701941} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701956} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701957} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701965} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701967} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705162} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705171} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705180} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705187} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705219} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705221} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705223} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705238}] :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expressions in Radians Using the Sum and Difference Formulas"} :step/id #uuid "23953749-c368-59ef-b666-9cb9c2e9f984" :step/math-academy-id 37601 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060806}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060806 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060866 :tutorial/content "Let's now prove the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(A+B) = \\sin A\\cos B + \\cos A\\sin B\n$$\n\nTo start with, we need to use the *difference* formula for *cosine*:\n\n$$\n\\cos(A-B) = \\cos A\\cos B + \\sin A\\sin B\n$$\n\nIf you haven't seen this formula yet, don't worry. You'll learn more about it, including how it's proved using the unit circle, in a separate lesson.\n\nNow, if we replace $A$ with $\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2} - A\\right)$ in the difference formula for cosine, we get\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(\\dfrac\\pi2 - A-B\\right) = \\cos \\left(\\dfrac\\pi2 - A\\right)\\cos B + \\sin\\left(\\dfrac\\pi2 - A\\right)\\sin B\n$$\n\ni.e.\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(\\dfrac\\pi2 - (A+B)\\right) = \\cos \\left(\\dfrac\\pi2 - A\\right)\\cos B + \\sin\\left(\\dfrac\\pi2 - A\\right)\\sin B.\n$$\n\nNext, using the cofunction identities\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-(A+B)\\right) & =\\operatorname{sin}(A+B) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-A\\right) & =\\operatorname{sin}A \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-A\\right) & =\\operatorname{cos}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe identity above reduces to\n\n$$\n\\sin(A+B) = \\sin A\\cos B + \\cos A\\sin B\n$$\n\nas required." :tutorial/id #uuid "27cf015f-7be2-50f5-aed3-a5dc1f2cb26e" :tutorial/math-academy-id 13284 :tutorial/title "Proving the Sum Formula"} :step/id #uuid "7ca2f832-c9fe-56ac-bb63-b51f4bfb5a79" :step/math-academy-id 461995 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060807}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060807 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060867 :tutorial/content "We have shown how to derive the sum formula\n\n$$\n\\sin(A+B) = \\sin A\\cos B + \\cos A\\sin B.\n$$\n\nWe can derive the difference formula for sine by simply replacing $B$ with $-B,$ and using the evenness/oddness identities for cosine and sine, respectively:\n\n$$\n\\cos(-B) = \\cos B, \\qquad \\sin(-B) = -\\sin B\n$$\n\nSubstituting these into our sum formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}(A+(-B))=\\operatorname{sin}A\\operatorname{cos}(-B)+\\operatorname{cos}A\\operatorname{sin}(-B)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\sin(A-B) = \\sin A\\cos B - \\cos A\\sin B\n$$\n\nas required." :tutorial/id #uuid "93e513c3-90cf-588d-84a3-ed0b82e82401" :tutorial/math-academy-id 13285 :tutorial/title "Proving the Difference Formula"} :step/id #uuid "abef5a7a-78f9-5491-81b5-f9c42898d085" :step/math-academy-id 461996}] :activity/title "The Sum and Difference Formulas for Sine" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059945}]}
